# SYNTHETIC INPUT: nothing here is from the recording and nothing is the owner's input.
# Written by the planner on 12 October 2026 (NOTES.md, 09:0x): the player switches to another
# application during play and comes back (the host window stops being the key window, then
# is it again), twice, with a key held across the first.  Found by a hidden run, not by him:
# what the game does when Windows tells it that it is no longer in front.
#
#   GATE3_INPUT_SCRIPT=gate3/synthetic/away.script build/gate3/gate3 run
#
# The first two sections are continue.script's, unchanged.  Times are milliseconds after the
# anchor fired.

anchor mark main-menu
3000 moveto 375 577
3400 button left down
3480 button left up

anchor mark mission-frame
5000 key down 32
5120 key up 32

# 20 s into play: W held, the window loses the foreground for 3 s, comes back, W released.
20000 key down 87
20500 active off
23500 active on
24000 key up 87

# A second, short absence, then a right click and a double tap as proof that input lives.
26000 active off
26300 active on
28000 button right down
28300 button right up
29000 button left down
29080 button left up
29200 button left down
29280 button left up
